      "body": "Fixes #37639\n\n## Motivation\n\n`Spark2_5Attention` hardcodes `torch.sigmoid` for the per-head attention\noutput gate, ignoring the config field `gate_attn_act_mode` that the\nreference implementation (`modeling_spark.py`) honors with `sigmoid` and\n`silu` branches (and a `ValueError` for anything else). Both released\nSpark-X2.5 checkpoints declare `\"sigmoid\"`, so there is no divergence\ntoday, but any future checkpoint declaring `\"silu\"` would silently get\nthe wrong gate activation (bounded, strictly positive `sigmoid` instead\nof unbounded `silu`, which goes negative for `x < 0`), with the error\ncompounding across every attention layer and no error pointing at the\ncause.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/configs/spark2_5.py`: declare `gate_attn_act_mode`\n  (default `\"sigmoid\"`, matching the released checkpoints and preserving\n  current behavior for configs that omit the field).\n- `python/sglang/srt/models/spark2_5.py`:\n  - `Spark2_5Attention` takes `gate_attn_act_mode` (default `\"sigmoid\"`)\n    and validates it at construction, raising `ValueError` for\n    unsupported modes when the gate is enabled, so a bad config fails\n    fast at load time instead of silently serving wrong activations.\n  - `forward` applies `F.silu` when the mode is `\"silu\"` and keeps the\n    existing `torch.sigmoid` path otherwise.\n  - `Spark2_5DecoderLayer` forwards `getattr(config,\n    \"gate_attn_act_mode\", \"sigmoid\")` to the attention module.\n\n## Tests\n\nNo GPU and no torch on this machine, so the change could not be run\nthrough a model forward pass here; that verification is left to CI:\n\n- A stub harness executed the actual activation-selection lines\n  extracted from `forward` (via AST, not a copy) against a minimal\n  fake tensor: the `sigmoid` branch and the `silu` branch both match\n  the reference activations exactly on `[-6, -2, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 2, 6]`.\n- The same harness checks the `__init__` default (`\"sigmoid\"`), the\n  unsupported-mode `ValueError`, the decoder-layer config forwarding,\n  and the config-class field.\n- `ruff check --select F401,F821,F823,UP037`, `ruff format --check`,\n  `python3 -m py_compile`, and `git diff --check` all pass on both\n  touched files. No existing test covers `spark2_5` gate behavior\n  (checked the test tree), so no test contradicts the new behavior.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40097789744](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40097789744)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40097789675](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40097789675)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40097789805](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40097789805)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
